# Cloudflare deploy

Two Workers ship from this repo: the **web** app (`apps/web`, Next.js via OpenNext) and the **cron** Worker (`apps/cron`, Hono). Both bind the same D1 database (`DB`) and R2 bucket (`STORAGE`).

## One-time provisioning
1. **D1:** `wrangler d1 create {{projectName}}-db` → copy the returned `database_id` into the `"database_id"` field of **both** `apps/web/wrangler.jsonc` and `apps/cron/wrangler.jsonc` (they share one database).
2. **R2:** `wrangler r2 bucket create {{projectName}}-storage` (and `{{projectName}}-storage-preview` if you use `wrangler dev` preview on the web app).
3. **Secrets** (the web app; the cron Worker has none): `apps/web/wrangler.jsonc` lists `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` under `secrets.required`, so a deploy fails until it is set. Run `wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` once the Worker exists; the first deploy of a new Worker takes it from a file instead, see below. Set `BETTER_AUTH_URL` (the public URL of the web app) as a `vars` entry in `apps/web/wrangler.jsonc` or with `wrangler secret put BETTER_AUTH_URL`. Public values (e.g. `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`) stay in `.env` at build time, not secrets.
4. **Remote migrations:** `cd packages/db && {{runScript "db:migrate:remote"}}` to apply the schema to the live D1 database.

## Build & deploy
- **Web:** `cd apps/web && {{runScript "build:cf"}}` (wrangler types → `opennextjs-cloudflare build`, which runs `next build` once through the `build` script) then `cd apps/web && {{runScript "deploy"}}` (`opennextjs-cloudflare deploy`). The first deploy of a new Worker takes the secrets from a file: `cd apps/web && {{runScript "deploy"}} -- --secrets-file .prod.env` (`.prod.env` is gitignored).
- **Build where `.env` holds no real secret.** `build:cf` bundles every `.env*` value, server secrets included, into the Worker (`.open-next/cloudflare/next-env.mjs`) as a `process.env` fallback, with no opt-out. A secret set with `wrangler secret put` wins at runtime, but the bundled value is used silently when the secret was never set. Build the Worker you deploy in CI, or from a checkout without `apps/web/.env`.
- **Cron:** from `apps/cron`, `{{packageRunner}} wrangler deploy`. The `triggers.crons` schedule (`0 3 * * *` — daily at 03:00 UTC) is registered on deploy.

## Local development
- `cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env` and set `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` (any value locally; `BETTER_AUTH_URL` is already `http://localhost:3000`). Next.js reads `.env`; in dev mode Better Auth trusts `localhost`.
- `{{runScript "local-setup"}}` once (applies local migrations + seeds the local D1).
- `{{runScript "dev"}}` — `next dev` with the Cloudflare bindings wired via `initOpenNextCloudflareForDev` (D1/R2 from `.wrangler`, the same local state `local-setup` seeds). This is the primary local loop (hot reload, dev-mode auth).
- `cd apps/web && {{runScript "preview"}}` runs the OpenNext **production** build locally to smoke-test the deployed shape. The build freezes the values of `.env` into the Worker, so run `build:cf` again after every `.env` change. Wrangler does not load `.env` for this preview (OpenNext handles it), so it warns about a missing required `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` even when `.env` holds it; the warning is safe to ignore then.
- Fire the cron handler locally without waiting for the schedule: from `apps/cron`, `{{packageRunner}} wrangler dev --test-scheduled --persist-to ../../.wrangler` (the `--persist-to` makes it share the same local D1/R2 as the web app), then hit `http://localhost:<port>/__scheduled` to run `scheduled()` (purges expired documents from the local D1 + R2).

## Build-time vs runtime env
Bindings (`DB`, `STORAGE`) are **runtime**, read through `getEnv()` (web) or the `Env` arg (cron), never at module load. Secrets are runtime too: set them with `wrangler secret put`, never rely on `.env`, whose values are bundled into the Worker at build. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` and other build-time config come from `.env`. Keep the D1/R2 access request- or event-scoped; see [Data layer](data-layer.md) and [Storage](storage.md).
